# The hand-upload archives from CLAUDE.md §8 — `cd dist && zip -r ../<name>.zip .`. Each is
# a repacked copy of `dist/`, which is itself ignored two lines up, so tracking one would put
# a 400KB binary in the history on every deploy that carries no information the source does
# not already carry. Regenerate them, never fetch one from a commit.
#
# A pattern rather than a filename: the rule named `site.zip` alone and the very next archive
# was `tiffsoftwaresolutionswebsiteV1.zip`, which walked straight past it. These get renamed
# per version by whoever is uploading — `tiffsoftwarewebsite20260822.zip` is still sitting in
# the docroot from August — so the name is exactly the part that cannot be relied on.
#
# Anchored to the repo root, so a zip that is ever genuinely part of the site (a download on
# a page, say, under `public/`) is still tracked.
/*.zip
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
